      "widgets_values": [
        "integrated_multimodal_description: Use <Picture 1> as the character identity reference for Mario: red M cap, large nose, black moustache, red shirt, blue overalls, white gloves and brown shoes, with the same bold black outlines and colorful cartoon design. Use <Picture 2> as the castle reference: a small brown brick castle with a wide lower wall, a centered dark arched doorway, crenellated battlements and a narrower square tower above. Keep the castle's recognizable shape and brick pattern. Create a playful single continuous ten-second scene on a light tabletop, with Mario small enough to fit through the castle doorway. The castle stays fully visible in the middle of the frame. During the first three seconds Mario walks in from the left toward the castle. During seconds three to six he stops beside the doorway, turns toward the camera and waves cheerfully. During seconds six to ten he turns back, walks through the doorway and disappears inside, leaving the castle visible. Preserve Mario's identity and the castle throughout. Wide stationary camera, coherent gentle movement, no cuts, no additional characters, no captions. The two pictures are independent identity and object references, not start or end frames.\noverall_soundscape: Light footsteps on the tabletop, a soft swish during the wave, quiet indoor ambience. No dialogue.\nnon_diegetic_music: None.\n"
